# {{dist_name}}

{{description}}

An [Aevion](https://pypi.org/project/aevion/) plugin. After `pip install -e ".[test]"` the components below are
available in every Aevion configuration, with no code changes on the user's side:

| Registry | Name | What it does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| sensors | `{{component}}` | {{class_name}}: a downward range sensor (altitude above ground with noise and a range limit) |
| hooks | `{{component}}_log` | prints vehicle 0's altitude once per simulated second |

```yaml
schema_version: 1
duration: 5
sensors:
  - type: {{component}}
    params: {max_range: 8.0}
hooks:
  - type: {{component}}_log
```

```bash
aevion plugins          # shows this plugin and whether it loaded
aevion registry sensors # lists '{{component}}' with source '{{package}}'
aevion run config.yaml
```

## Develop

```bash
pip install -e ".[test]"
pytest
```

The plugin mechanism is described in Aevion's `docs/plugins.md`. Plugins run with the user's privileges: only install
plugins you trust (`AEVION_DISABLE_PLUGINS=1` skips plugin loading).
